# M3 walkthrough: tasks, the board, live events, and the chief assigning work.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisite: the research department with a lead and a web specialist (see m2-org.http).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@departmentId = paste-the-research-department-id

### Watch live events in a terminal while you go (Ctrl+C to stop). Add -H "Last-Event-ID: <seq>" to replay.
# curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://127.0.0.1:4111/v1/events

### Give the research department a task. It goes straight to the lead (dispatch defaults to true).
# @name task
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "departmentId": "{{departmentId}}",
  "title": "What is Mastra?",
  "brief": "Find out what the Mastra framework is. Two sentences, with one source URL.",
  "priority": "normal"
}

### Follow it: phase, checklist, progress and, once reported, the result
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{task.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Its history: created, dispatched, progress, reported, chief_notified...
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{task.response.body.id}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deliverables the lead attached
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{task.response.body.id}}/artifacts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The board: open tasks and this week's closed ones, by phase
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/board?departmentId={{departmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ask for changes: a task in review goes back to the lead with your message
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{task.response.body.id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "Add a second source, please.", "mode": "steer" }

### Accept it once it's back in review
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{task.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phase": "done" }

### Park a task without sending it, then send it later with PATCH { "phase": "queued" }
# @name parked
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "departmentId": "{{departmentId}}", "title": "Compare agent frameworks", "brief": "Mastra versus two others.", "dispatch": false }

### Cancel it (stops the lead if it is working on it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{parked.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Not needed after all" }

### Or let the chief of staff assign the work. The conversation lives on the chief:main thread.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/chief/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Have research find out who maintains Mastra, with a source." }],
  "memory": { "thread": "chief:main", "resource": "owner" }
}

### The chief's thread, including the notifications it received when leads reported
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/memory/threads/chief:main/messages?agentId=chief
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
